Subject: Cantor Identity Accounting Store Bootstrap P3 Justification

@ [justification_uuid] afe56288-7e2a-40fb-b7d8-ce4d5ba0a00b

& [Why]
  + P2 safely resumes an existing journal but leaves creation of its first snapshot to an embedding caller
  + a separate one-shot bootstrap keeps initial authority visible and prevents the long-running MCP tool from acquiring fuzzy admission or overwrite powers

& [WhyThisShape]
  + canonical IdentityLedger input reuses P0 object accounting rather than inventing a second seed schema
  + absent-directory creation and post-write reload provide a narrow operator transaction with a testable success boundary

& [Rejected]
  + server auto-initialization because a typo could silently create a second identity history
  + natural-language object creation because linguistic plausibility is not objective admission
  + overwrite or merge because both require separately governed migration and conflict semantics
